 - source_spec: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-3-1-text-entry-capture-insertion-modal-shell.md`
   summary: Swipe-down and scrim-tap can still dismiss the Insertion Modal while a save is in flight (`POST /entries` already sent), silently creating the entry with no user-visible confirmation.
   evidence: The "x" close button and tab bar are being patched to disable during `TextEntrySaving`, but Flutter's built-in `showModalBottomSheet` swipe-to-dismiss/barrier-tap gestures aren't easily gated per-state the same way (would need a reactive `isDismissible`/`PopScope`-style guard). Low-frequency path — the entry is still correctly created and cached — but worth a dedicated fix if it proves disruptive in practice.
+- source_spec: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-3-1-text-entry-capture-insertion-modal-shell.md`
+  summary: A local Hive-box write failure that happens *after* `entries-create` has already succeeded server-side maps to `Left(Failure.malformedResponse(...))` in `EntriesRepositoryImpl.create` — the same outcome as a genuine network/parse failure — so the cubit re-enables Salvar and invites a retry that fires a second, un-deduplicated `entries-create` call.
+  evidence: `lib/features/entries/data/repositories/entries_repository_impl.dart:42-46`. The epic's own idempotency note (`epic-3-context.md`: "`create` on the port is idempotent on `(origin, chatMessageId)`, though that specific guard only matters starting with RF10") already scopes general duplicate-entry risk as out of this story's concern — this is the same accepted risk surfacing through a different trigger (a local disk failure instead of a user retry after a network failure). Revisit alongside that RF10 idempotency work, or sooner if local Hive write failures prove non-negligible in practice.
+- source_spec: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-3-1-text-entry-capture-insertion-modal-shell.md`
+  summary: `Failure.malformedResponse(message: error.toString())` is used in both `entries_remote_data_source.dart`'s parse-failure catch and `entries_repository_impl.dart`'s Hive-write-failure catch, surfacing a raw Dart exception string (e.g. `"FormatException: ..."`) as the inline/announced message a user sees or hears.
+  evidence: `lib/features/entries/data/datasources/entries_remote_data_source.dart:37`, `lib/features/entries/data/repositories/entries_repository_impl.dart:45`. Pre-existing project-wide pattern, not introduced by this story — `entries_repository_impl.dart`'s own comment cites `AuthRepositoryImpl`'s identical fallback, and this file's story-1-3 entry already flags the same raw-English-string gap for `ApiClient`'s own fallback messages. No `Failure`→localized-copy mapping layer exists anywhere yet; revisit once more than one screen needs curated failure copy, same as that earlier entry recommends.
+- source_spec: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-3-1-text-entry-capture-insertion-modal-shell.md`
+  summary: `EntriesRepositoryImpl.create`'s Hive-write-failure catch reuses `Failure.malformedResponse`, whose own doc comment scopes it to "a 200 response that doesn't match the expected shape" (a parse failure) — not a local disk/Hive I/O failure, which is a different cause entirely.
+  evidence: `lib/features/entries/data/repositories/entries_repository_impl.dart:45`, `lib/core/failure/failure.dart:36-39`. Satisfies RNF09 ("no exception escapes unmapped") and is the least-wrong fit in the closed 14-member `Failure` hierarchy, not an oversight — but no current code branches on `Failure` subtype (only `.message`/`.retryable` are read), so there's no observable bug today. Revisit if a future feature needs to distinguish "local persistence failed" from "server sent something we couldn't parse."
+- source_spec: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-3-1-text-entry-capture-insertion-modal-shell.md`
+  summary: An exception thrown by the new `Hive.initFlutter()`/`registerEntriesFeature()` calls during app bootstrap propagates out of `setupCoreDependencies()` uncaught — `main.dart`'s own `try`/`catch` around that call only logs and `rethrow`s, so the app still crashes with no fallback UI.
+  evidence: `lib/core/di/injection_container.dart:90-92`, `lib/main.dart:17-26`. Pre-existing behavior, not introduced by this story — every one of the five feature registrations `setupCoreDependencies()` already performs (auth/vault/account, now entries/capture) shares the exact same fatal-crash-on-failure contract, and `main.dart`'s catch block's own message is already `.env`-specific wording predating this diff. Revisit only as part of a deliberate app-wide bootstrap-resilience decision, not a one-off fix for the Hive call alone.
+- source_spec: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/spec-3-1-text-entry-capture-insertion-modal-shell.md`
+  summary: `EntrySource.audio`/`EntrySource.photo` are never exercised through `EntriesRemoteDataSource`/`EntriesRepositoryImpl`'s real serialization or Hive round-trip — only `manual` (this story) and `chat` are covered.
+  evidence: `test/features/entries/data/datasources/entries_remote_data_source_test.dart`, `test/features/entries/data/repositories/entries_repository_impl_integration_test.dart`. `EntrySource` was deliberately widened to all 4 values now so Stories 3.2/3.3 reuse this exact datasource/repository method unchanged (Code Map) — those stories are the natural place to add their own `audio`/`photo` coverage once they actually produce those sources, rather than writing speculative tests for values nothing calls yet.
